### Travelling Salesman Problem Model

The following Minizinc model solves the Travelling Salesman Problem (TSP) using the given locations.

```minizinc
% TSP Model

% Input data
int: num_cities = 12;
array[1..num_cities] of tuple(int, int): locations = [
    (288, 149), (288, 129), (270, 133), (256, 141), (256, 163), (246, 157),
    (236, 169), (228, 169), (228, 148), (220, 164), (212, 172), (204, 159)
];

% Calculate the distance matrix
array[1..num_cities, 1..num_cities] of var float: distance_matrix;
constraint forall(i in 1..num_cities, j in 1..num_cities) (
    if i == j then
        distance_matrix[i, j] = 0
    else
        let {
            int: x_diff = locations[i, 1] - locations[j, 1],
            int: y_diff = locations[i, 2] - locations[j, 2]
        } in
            distance_matrix[i, j] = sqrt(int2float(x_diff * x_diff + y_diff * y_diff))
    endif
);

% TSP variables
array[1..num_cities] of var 1..num_cities: tour;
var float: travel_distance;

% Constraints
constraint circuit(tour);
constraint travel_distance = sum(i in 1..num_cities-1)(distance_matrix[tour[i], tour[i+1]]) + distance_matrix[tour[num_cities], tour[1]];

% Solve
solve minimize travel_distance;

% Output
output [
    "{",
    join(",", [
        "\"travel_distance\": " ++ show(travel_distance)
    ]),
    "}"
];
```

