2. **Column Constraint**: For each column `j`, the sum of `x[i, j]` over all rows `i` should be 14. This can be represented as `sum([x[i, j] | i in 1..31]) = 14` for `j in 1..31`.
3. **Objective Function**: The sum of the quadratic horizontal distance from the main diagonal for all cells containing a coin can be calculated as `sum([x[i, j] * (i - j) * (i - j) | i in 1..31, j in 1..31])`. This will be our objective function `z` to minimize.

